  "chain": "new TXV #1 internals binding with original valve body [cause B] -> TXV #1 stuck closed -> compressor deprived of refrigerant, trips on high discharge temperature -> (parallel: inadequate post-maintenance testing strategy failed to detect degraded condition) -> SGK05A Class 1E A/C train inoperable, TS 3.7.20 Required Actions not entered in time [backup: supplemental cooling system, B-train A/C operable]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Inoperability was determined retrospectively to have begun at 1530 on 10/25/22 (when frosting/condensation first observed), not at the 10/27/22 trip; both dates are captured in the consequence window. Two contributing causes (new valve internals binding with original body; inadequate PMT strategy) modeled as separate FailureMode nodes feeding the same consequence in parallel per rule 5. Supplemental cooling system and B-train A/C are explicitly stated as operable/available during the event window, so BACKED_UP_BY is asserted for supplemental cooling (B-train A/C omitted as separate System node since it is the redundant train of the same system, not a distinct backup system)."
